From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yaniss <yaniss91600@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 13:25:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] cuda: skip fully-masked KV tiles in flash attention

DeepSeek-V4-Flash builds a sparse attention mask from a top-k indexer, so
most KV tiles of a query tile are entirely masked out. A prepass
(flash_attn_mask_to_KV_skip) builds a per-tile bitmap of empty stride
blocks; the kernels consume it and skip those tiles outright.

Skipping a fully-masked tile is exact in floating point: KQ_max is
unchanged, scale = expf(0) = 1, KQ_sum gains 0 and VKQ is multiplied by
1. The output is bit-identical to the dense path, which is how the
change is gated.

Measured on gfx1151 (Strix Halo, ROCm), server prefill: +21.6% at 11k
context, +13.1% at 40k. The gain decays with depth because the skip is
tile-granular and tile density rises (57.9% empty tiles at 11k, 32.7% at
40k).

Note that on gfx1151 the selected kernel is always fattn-tile:
ggml_cuda_get_best_fattn_kernel gates amd_wmma_available on
Q->ne[0] <= 128 while DKQ = 576. The fattn-mma-f16 side of this change
is therefore inert there and is only exercised on NVIDIA.

Also adds flash_attn_mask_to_KV_rows, a row-granular variant of the same
prepass. It is reachable only through DSV4_FA_ROW_STATS, which reports
the size of the union it would produce without consuming it.
